      "message": "Let a person save a repository, and keep the sidebar their own\n\nThe sidebar listed every public repository on the forge for everyone,\nwhich is a list of the forge, not of the person. Repositories now\nlists what is yours to work in: your own, your organisations', and\nthose you hold a grant on. Anything else you may read, you save from\nits page and it sits under Saved until you let it go; saving is yours\nalone, an operational table rather than the log, following a rename\nand a deletion. The API says the same: bookmark, unbookmark, and what\nyou saved. Settings opens with an Account panel that says your\nusername and display name, since the name the forge calls you by was\nshown nowhere; it cannot be changed yet, and the panel says so.\n\nTask: t-5g0z3gqe9s2rstrjasc9tv677e\nChange-Id: Isaved0128\nSigned-off-by: Mandip Adhikari <92096340+mandipadk@users.noreply.github.com>",
